<urn:atm:triage:finding/DEBUG-ASSERT-REDUNDANT-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "DEBUG-ASSERT-REDUNDANT-001" ;
  triage:title "redundant debug_assert! in apply_display_mutations_to_store strictly subsumed by following debug_assert_eq!" ;
  triage:description "Prior finding reported a redundant debug_assert!(own_inbox || ack_activation_mode == AckActivationMode::ReadOnly) at apply_display_mutations_to_store that was strictly subsumed by the following debug_assert_eq!(ack_activation_mode, AckActivationMode::ReadOnly). Current sweep confirms the redundant assertion has been removed across all branches. The own_inbox parameter is now marked unused (_own_inbox). Only the debug_assert_eq! remains at line 859." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AD" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "CODE" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:fixedOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/AD32/46be50b0> ;
  triage:fixedOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/AD33/6ef24f32> ;
  triage:fixedOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/AD34/05ddab01> ;
  triage:fixedOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/AD35/afdaf3c5> ;
  triage:notes "CONFLICT RESOLVED - INDEPENDENT VERIFICATION (2026-07-10): AD35-QA-2 incorrectly reported finding 'confirmed still present at read/mod.rs:859', but independent verification confirms TRIAGE-3 summary was correct: finding is CLOSED on AD.32-35. The confusion arose from misinterpreting the correct debug_assert_eq!(ack_activation_mode, AckActivationMode::ReadOnly) at line 859 as the redundant assertion still being present. FACTS: (1) Redundant assertion debug_assert!(own_inbox || ack_activation_mode == AckActivationMode::ReadOnly) is ABSENT from all four branches; (2) Function parameter own_inbox renamed to _own_inbox (marked unused) on all branches; (3) Only correct debug_assert_eq! remains at line 859 on all branches; (4) Pattern consistent across AD.32 (46be50b0), AD.33 (6ef24f32), AD.34 (05ddab01), AD.35 (afdaf3c5). Severity dispute noted in prior triage (AD32-QA-2 marked BLOCKING, AD34-QA-1 and AD35-QA-2 mark MINOR). Finding definitively fixed and propagated across all phase-AD branches. Status: FIXED." .

